    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0293" n="181" xml:id="pg181"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20261/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-04T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 4, 1919,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 5, 11:55
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3794. Referring to your 1581, March 27th. I have seen the Swedish Foreign Office
                    in regard to Lomonossoff and they have cabled the Swedish Legation in Washington
                    instructions to grant him a vise to permit his entry into Sweden. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
